WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.956
Question two: an installed solution is not always a working one.

2
00:00:04.956 --> 00:00:11.790
In this demonstration I check the school's agents against the six operational checks in the SOP.

3
00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:13.072
It is nine thirty.

4
00:00:14.172 --> 00:00:16.468
The six checks, B1 to B6.

5
00:00:16.468 --> 00:00:17.938
Service running.

6
00:00:17.938 --> 00:00:21.521
Real-time protection on, for antivirus.

7
00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:24.920
A check-in in the last sixty minutes.

8
00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:31.442
Content no more than three days old, so dated November second or later.

9
00:00:31.442 --> 00:00:33.279
A supported version.

10
00:00:33.279 --> 00:00:35.576
And tamper protection on.

11
00:00:35.576 --> 00:00:38.700
One failure means not operational.

12
00:00:39.799 --> 00:00:44.239
The health export, as a table on the Windows workstation.

13
00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:50.564
DH-1 passes everything.

14
00:00:50.564 --> 00:00:57.017
DH-2 is the antivirus on the registrar's PC: running, real-time on,

15
00:00:57.017 --> 00:01:02.795
but its signatures are from October thirtieth, six days old.

16
00:01:02.795 --> 00:01:08.188
It fails B4, so it cannot recognise this week's malware.

17
00:01:08.188 --> 00:01:15.892
DH-3, the EDR on the same PC, is stopped and has not checked in since six forty.

18
00:01:15.892 --> 00:01:17.722
It fails B1 and B3.

19
00:01:17.722 --> 00:01:18.878
DH-4 passes.

20
00:01:19.978 --> 00:01:24.637
So the registrar's PC, a Tier 1 computer with student records,

21
00:01:24.637 --> 00:01:29.146
is protected by an out-of-date antivirus and no working EDR.

22
00:01:29.146 --> 00:01:34.858
Two lines in the report, both to the Shift Lead, each with its failed check.

23
00:01:35.958 --> 00:01:36.869
Your turn.

24
00:01:36.869 --> 00:01:41.791
In the CTM Virtual Lab, choose Day 7 and Activity 7.2.

25
00:01:41.791 --> 00:01:44.982
Fourteen agent checks for the bank.

26
00:01:44.982 --> 00:01:47.990
Apply all six checks to each one.

27
00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:53.003
One failure is explained by something you did on Day 5.

28
00:01:53.003 --> 00:01:54.462
Can you find it?

